course: dictionary
lesson: 14325
title: Observable: can it be seen?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «Observable» comes from «observe», which means to look at carefully. Something observable is able to be seen or noticed. You can often work out the meaning from the word parts: observ-able means you are able to observe it.
explain: In science, the word has a stricter job. «The colour of the liquid changed from blue to green, which was observable.» An observable fact is one you can check by looking, measuring or testing, so a scientist can see it, measure it or test it.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a simpler word. «The bubbles were observable» becomes «The bubbles were able to be seen». If the sentence still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Observable means able to be seen or noticed.
fact: In science, an observable fact is one you can check by looking, measuring or testing.
fact: «Observable» comes from «observe», which means to look at carefully.
fact: Examples of observable changes in an experiment are a colour change, bubbles, or a rise in temperature.
fact: In astronomy, the observable universe is the part of space we can see or detect from Earth.
exercise: «The colour change in the test tube was observable.» What does observable mean here? | Made of metal | Very cold to touch | *Able to be seen | Too small to measure
exercise: A scientist writes, «The bubbles were observable.» What does this tell us? | They were made of sugar | They were hidden inside the glass | *They could be seen | They were never there at all
exercise: Which fact is observable? | The ice cube felt lonely | *The ice cube melted into water | The ice cube had a secret wish | The ice cube was thinking about summer
test:
«The gas bubbles were observable through the glass.» What does observable mean? | *Able to be seen | Able to be eaten | Hidden inside the glass | Too heavy to lift
Which of these is an observable change in an experiment? | Bubbles rising in the liquid | The scientist's favourite food | *A colour change in the liquid | A thought in the scientist's head
exam: Mia says observable means hidden. What does observable really mean? | *Able to be seen or noticed | Very quiet and still | Made of glass | Hidden from view
